  "body": "## What\n\nAdds `doc/2026-11-08_design_id5847.md` — the decision-ready design record for importing a **Logseq** graph into the #2048 object model, as issue #5847 asks: chosen shape, rejected alternatives, implementation invariants, round-trip export expectations, and a test corpus plan.\n\nDesign only; no importer code.\n\n## Shape\n\nIt follows the sibling Joplin importer design (`doc/2026-11-08_design_id5848.md`, #5848) so the importer family stays one design with per-source deltas. §0 lists the Logseq deltas:\n\n- **Pages are the note unit; blocks are not notes.** Blocks are outline structure inside a page's revision, carried as an explicit block tree with manifest-scoped identity. A note per block would flood the graph and destroy page-level revision history.\n- **`((block-uuid))` needs stable block identity.** Carried as a typed reference to the owning note plus a pinned block identity in the manifest, so export can rebuild the reference exactly.\n- **Daily-journal pages are notes with a journal-date claim**, not a second note type.\n- **Page and block properties map to claims**; namespaced pages are alias claims, not collections.\n- **Stated lossy list:** query blocks, templates/macros, whiteboards, plugin data, dynamic variables, block-level revision history.\n\n## The one parent-decision touch (§7)\n\n#2048's typed references target notes and optionally pin revisions; Logseq references target blocks. This design adds no new reference kind and declines to re-decide #2048 on an importer ticket — if native block backlinks are wanted, that is a #2048 amendment, and §7 names the paragraph to amend.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Docs-only change: no code, no tests to run.\n- Checked against current `main` (6f1efc4424): no existing Logseq design record, no open PR for #5847, and #2048's design landed 2026-11-07 (PR #3885).\n\nCloses #5847\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796734004&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7689&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7689&signature=b917c84b016572c1956d88e3ed9216a2ad458e4907e04e3bad39673a8da6893d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7689?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
